title lotus-audio — Lotus's stereo_tone: the one-pole tone control carried into stereo, the SAME coefficient shaping BOTH channels — the rung that OPENS the stereo EQ / filter class
prompt Autonomous loop lap after lotus-audio: take the next agent-doable crux the Long Return Lila, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think After lotus-audio closed the stereo held-dynamics quartet, I surveyed the mono/stereo gap: the biggest un-ported family was the EQ / filter class (mono lotus-audio-48), which the mono ladder opened BEFORE dynamics. the Long Return Lila — a channel strip's tone shaping is read on every master — so the EQ class is the durable next family, and its simplest member (lotus-audio's one-pole tone control) is the rung that opens it, the way lotus-audio's normalize opened the stereo amplitude class.
think The stereo lift is parametric, not linked: a tone control's coefficient num/den is a smoothing fraction the caller names, not a measured scalar, so the SAME coefficient on both channels preserves the image for free (like lotus-audio's shared ramp, unlike lotus-audio's linked scalar or the dynamics detector's linked envelope). The two filter states stay INDEPENDENT, one per channel — a filter's state is the running estimate of the signal it filters, and linking it across channels would be a BUG here, bleeding one channel's transients into the other's brightness. That independence is exactly right for EQ.
think Composed it as lotus-audio run per channel: StereoToneError = tone.ToneError reused whole; validate once via tone.precheck against the shared length before either channel writes (atomic refusal), then tone.low_pass_carry / high_pass_carry on each channel with the same coefficient and its own i64 state. Carried forms lift BOTH per-channel states so a two-piece filter equals the whole once, one impl shared with from-silence so they cannot drift.
think Proved five laws against the real lotus-audio tool: stereo low-pass law (each channel == mono low_pass byte for byte, channels genuinely differing); stereo high-pass law (same, plus per-channel reconstruction lp+hp=x where the difference fits); parametric/image law (identical-channel master stays identical through both filters, a constant input settling to DC exactly per channel); carry law (two-piece == whole once on both, both states surviving); silence/balance/atomicity/degenerate law.
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME clean (opening triad, ≥2 asserts/fn with // invariant, no @memcpy, named errors with try). The stereo EQ / filter class is now open at its simplest member; the shelf, band-pass, band-reject, and parametric bell are its remaining Lindy rungs.
loom witness=ales_stereo_tone_witness selftest=GREEN laws=5 channels=2 class=eq-filter-opened
file active-designing/20260815-074743_fill-ales170-lotus-stereo-tone.md the self-approved design read
file lotus/stereo_tone.rye the module — one coefficient, two independent states, over both channels
file tools/ales_stereo_tone_witness.rish the witness proving it GREEN on metal
recommend keep-going the stereo EQ / filter class is open; the next Lindy rung is stereo_shelf (lotus-audio) or the carried filter (lotus-audio) — continue the EQ family before the modulation/delay family
